{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Encounter.MostowTriangulationBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowTriangulationBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Encounter.MostowRigidity","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ManifoldVolumeBridge"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowTriangulationBridge.volumeInvariant_eq_of_two_realisations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowTriangulationBridge.volumeInvariant_eq_of_two_realisations","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowTriangulationBridge.lean#L108-L121","doc":"**Any two triangulations realising a Mostow-rigid manifold agree with its\ninvariant.**\n\nThe well-definedness statement in the form the Mostow module can consume: it is\nthe invariant, not merely some real, that both sums compute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowTriangulationBridge.figureEight_volume_eq_triangulation_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowTriangulationBridge.figureEight_volume_eq_triangulation_volume","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowTriangulationBridge.lean#L80-L106","doc":"**The figure-eight invariant IS the computed Bloch–Wigner sum.**\n\nRESOLVED 2026-08-30 (bean `qou-f8lit`). This theorem previously concluded\n`(2.02988321281930 : ℝ) = T.volume`, keyed on the decimal literal\n`MostowRigidity.figureEight` used to carry, and was **unusable at the figure-eight**:\nthat literal is a 15-digit truncation, `figureEightTriangulation.volume = VOL_4_1` is\nproved sorry-free, and the two differ at the 16th digit — so its hypotheses were jointly\nunsatisfiable there and no correct bridge instance could ever discharge them.\n\nThe instance is now exact (`volume := VOL_4_1`), so the statement is keyed on the exact\nconstant and applies. **The typechecker made the defect visible at exactly this line**:\nbefore exactification `volumeInvariant FigureEight` was *definitionally* the literal, so\nthe coercion went through silently; afterwards Lean reported\n\n    has type      volumeInvariant FigureEight = T.volume\n    but expected  2.02988321281930 = T.volume\n\nwhich is the whole finding in one error message. Worth remembering: a truncated literal\nstanding in for an exact constant is invisible while it is the definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Encounter.MostowTriangulationBridge.mostow_volume_eq_triangulation_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Encounter.MostowTriangulationBridge.mostow_volume_eq_triangulation_volume","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Encounter/MostowTriangulationBridge.lean#L62-L78","doc":"**The Mostow volume invariant equals the triangulation sum, under the bridge.**\n\nComposes three inputs: `compat` (the two notions agree), the bridge's transport\n`vol_eq_of_realises`, and the definition of `volumeInvariant`. None of them alone\ngives the conclusion.\n\n`compat` is an explicit argument rather than a class field on purpose — a field\nwould be inferred silently at every use site and would read as established. ","signatureChunk":0}]}